.TH GETCHAR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getchar \- read one byte from standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int getchar(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one byte from the Crunch standard input stream. This is a
function-like macro expanding to
.BR fgetc (stdin).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the byte as an integer from 0 to 255, or
.B EOF
(\-1) on end-of-file or error. Use
.BR feof (3crunch)
and
.BR ferror (3crunch)
to distinguish them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fgetc (3crunch),
.BR stdin (3crunch),
.BR putchar (3crunch)
